1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,870
What if all of
Earth's continents

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:05,010
joined into one
giant landmass?

3
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:07,030
It's happened
before:

4
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:09,530
Pangaea joined nearly
all land until

5
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:12,220
about two hundred
million years ago.

6
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:14,410
South America
and Africa

7
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:17,090
still fit like
puzzle pieces,

8
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:18,350
and plates
drift about

9
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:21,140
as fast as
fingernails grow.

10
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,440
One landmass changes
the weather.

11
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:27,140
Most moisture rises
from the sea,

12
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:28,880
so a supercontinent's
heart

13
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:31,270
would become a
vast desert.

14
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:34,200
People would crowd
the rainy coasts,

15
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,360
battered by
monsoons.

16
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:36,860
Inland,

17
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:40,190
days would scorch and
nights would freeze.

18
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:43,390
Animals from every
continent would meet,

19
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:45,750
and not all
would survive.

20
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:47,790
When the
Americas joined,

21
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:50,780
many South American
mammals vanished.

22
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:53,520
At sea, there'd be
far less coastline,

23
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,860
and fewer shallow,

24
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:58,710
sunlit waters where
coral reefs grow.

25
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:02,190
The next supercontinent
may be brutal:

26
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:04,030
one model finds
only eight

27
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:05,210
to sixteen percent

28
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:08,440
of its land livable
for mammals like us.

29
00:01:08,910 --> 00:01:11,450
Enjoy the map
while it lasts.

30
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:13,740
The continents
are still moving.
